en:
For one who has mastered the mind, the mind is the best friend;
for one who has not, it behaves like an enemy.
The same mind — the difference is who holds the reins.

hi:
जिसने मन को जीत लिया, उसका मन ही उसका सबसे अच्छा मित्र है;
जिसने नहीं जीता, उसके लिए वही मन शत्रु जैसा है।
मन वही है — फ़र्क़ बस इतना है कि लगाम किसके हाथ में है।

en:
Dwell on a thing, and attachment is born; from attachment, desire; from desire, anger;
and anger clouds judgment.
The chain is long — but it starts with where the mind lingers.

I went looking for the bad in others and found no one;
when I searched my own heart, I found no one worse than me.
Not self-blame — just the honest place where change begins.

As your desire is, so is your will; as your will is, so are your deeds;
and as your deeds are, so you become.
Choose tonight what you will feed.

hi:
जैसी कामना, वैसा संकल्प; जैसा संकल्प, वैसा कर्म;
और जैसा कर्म, वैसा ही आप बन जाते हैं।
आज रात चुनिए कि आप किसे पोसेंगे।

en:
Two birds sit on one tree. One eats the fruits, sweet and bitter;
the other simply watches.
Tonight, be the one who watches.
